# {{PROJECT}} Rationale store

This is MemContinuum's **Rationale** graph for {{PROJECT}}: the decision history behind the
codebase, not the codebase itself. `topics/<area>/<slug>.md` holds append-only chains of
rulings on one question each (newest link first); `incidents/<slug>.md` holds closed,
single-claim incident records; `investigations/` and `concepts/` are seeded but start empty.
This store is its own git repository -- never a subdirectory of a code repo it describes.

Schema: {{ENGINE_DIR}}/docs/SCHEMA.md. Engine: {{ENGINE_DIR}} (`memidx.py`, `memlint.py`).

## The citation rule, in six lines

1. Every ruling is a **link**, not a fact -- authority lives on the field, not the file.
2. `owner-verbatim` / `owner-ratified` = the owner's exact words, quoted, with a `source`
   pointer. This is the only tier that may block, refuse, or reverse work (a CONSTRAINT).
3. `agent-inference` / `reviewer-finding` / `code-derived` inform but never override a fix that
   code and tests already accept.
4. Never invent a quote. Never upgrade an authority because you believe it. Never merge two
   separately-dated statements into one "quote."
5. A changed mind is a **new link** (`reverses:` + `reason_for_change:`), never an edit to the
   old one. History is never rewritten, only superseded.
6. When in doubt about what a symbol/file is even allowed to do, ask `memidx.py why <symbol>` --
   it shows declined alternatives too, on purpose, before you "clean up" code that implements one.

## Running the engine

```bash
# One-time / after any edit to this store:
PYTHONPATH= {{PYTHON}} {{ENGINE_DIR}}/memlint.py {{STORE}} --code-root {{CODE_ROOT}}

PYTHONPATH= {{PYTHON}} {{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py reindex --root {{STORE}} --project {{PROJECT}}
# (index lands at ~/.memcontinuum/{{PROJECT}}.sqlite by default -- keep it on a local, POSIX
# filesystem, never a synced/cloud drive)

# Look things up:
{{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py chain <topic-id-or-slug> --project {{PROJECT}}
{{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py search "<question>" --mode hybrid --project {{PROJECT}}
{{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py for-path <file> --project {{PROJECT}}
{{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py why <symbol-or-path> --project {{PROJECT}} --code-root {{CODE_ROOT}}
{{ENGINE_DIR}}/memidx.py drift --code-root {{CODE_ROOT}} --project {{PROJECT}}
```

